WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.240 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.070
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.350 --> 01:24.080
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:29.880
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:42.570 --> 01:45.130
Don't go against me!

01:56.750 --> 01:59.620
No!

02:06.430 --> 02:07.430
<i>Cloud of Dust</i>

02:07.430 --> 02:11.330
<i>Cloud of Dust
Episode 17</i>

02:19.770 --> 02:20.700
Why you!

02:21.040 --> 02:23.270
Don't go against me!

02:27.110 --> 02:29.670
No!

02:31.680 --> 02:32.550
Naomi!

02:32.620 --> 02:34.250
Get it together, Naomi!

02:35.460 --> 02:39.050
That's why I'm telling you
not to go against me.

02:40.330 --> 02:41.690
You can't, Brother!

02:41.890 --> 02:45.130
Naoto Kirihara, you still don't get it?

02:51.300 --> 02:53.240
What's wrong, Naomi?

02:54.170 --> 02:56.700
Naoto, Naoya, why...

02:56.940 --> 02:58.910
Why did you have to die?

03:01.010 --> 03:03.880
No! It's a lie, a lie! Stop it!

03:04.050 --> 03:06.110
Naomi, please get it together.

03:06.390 --> 03:07.850
Stop it, Sonezaki!

03:08.390 --> 03:11.760
Then why don't you use
your power and stop me.

03:12.160 --> 03:15.320
I don't mind at all.

03:16.760 --> 03:18.820
I know. It's your fault...

03:18.900 --> 03:19.760
What?

03:20.000 --> 03:22.130
You were the one
that killed the kids!

03:22.200 --> 03:24.690
What are you saying, Naomi?

03:25.270 --> 03:27.830
You were the one that
made them go to the park!

03:27.940 --> 03:30.100
That's right. It's your fault!

03:30.740 --> 03:32.340
You killed them!

03:32.780 --> 03:34.580
Naomi, stop it!

03:34.680 --> 03:36.050
Idiot, idiot, idiot!

03:36.350 --> 03:38.040
Well, well...

03:38.120 --> 03:41.380
She had this kind of doubt
hidden inside of her for that long...

03:41.450 --> 03:45.980
...but was acting like this very loving
couple, huh? This is totally horrible...

03:47.160 --> 03:48.090
Stop!

03:50.900 --> 03:52.730
You really got mad, huh?

04:11.550 --> 04:12.810
There's no battery in it!

04:13.350 --> 04:15.250
How was he moving it?

04:18.830 --> 04:19.720
Honey!

04:20.130 --> 04:21.290
No!

04:32.410 --> 04:34.840
Naoto, Naoya! Are you okay?

04:35.840 --> 04:36.710
Naoya?

04:37.010 --> 04:38.140
You hit yourself?

04:38.210 --> 04:39.440
You're not hurt, are you?

04:42.220 --> 04:43.480
There, there...

05:00.000 --> 05:01.520
Stop it, Naoto!

05:03.300 --> 05:06.500
Do you remember those eyes now?

05:06.910 --> 05:10.430
How much you were
hated by your parents...

05:10.880 --> 05:14.810
You think they ever really loved you?

05:14.880 --> 05:17.680
Those two abandoned you.

05:17.750 --> 05:19.310
Shut up, don't talk anymore!

05:19.650 --> 05:22.780
Hey, hey, don't go commanding me.

05:23.790 --> 05:27.730
If you do anything more,
I will blow your head away!

05:27.960 --> 05:30.660
It's not my fault if you regret it.

05:31.000 --> 05:31.830
What!

05:32.400 --> 05:33.800
Brother, don't!

05:43.540 --> 05:46.170
T-There's something
wrong with these guys!

05:57.020 --> 05:57.890
No!

05:57.960 --> 05:59.620
It's not me, I'm...

06:03.760 --> 06:04.990
Stop it!

06:05.060 --> 06:07.060
Please forgive me!

06:07.130 --> 06:09.000
You're a monster.

06:09.070 --> 06:11.500
Monster!

06:11.670 --> 06:13.000
Damn it!

06:13.540 --> 06:15.200
Brother, no...

06:26.090 --> 06:29.050
What did you just do?

06:30.820 --> 06:32.020
Look!

06:32.090 --> 06:34.250
These guys are scared of you.

06:34.330 --> 06:37.020
So what are you going to do, Naoto?

06:39.570 --> 06:40.550
Please leave!

06:40.630 --> 06:43.430
We beg you, please leave right now!

06:45.070 --> 06:46.500
D-Dad...

06:49.210 --> 06:50.440
What did you say?

06:52.910 --> 06:54.880
What did you say just now?

06:57.080 --> 06:59.450
He does look like Naoya.

07:00.050 --> 07:01.310
That can't be!

07:02.150 --> 07:03.180
Naoya...

07:04.690 --> 07:05.920
Mom...

07:09.330 --> 07:12.660
Shucks, it's an annoying melodrama...

07:15.870 --> 07:16.890
What is it?

07:19.040 --> 07:20.230
Sonezaki!

07:21.370 --> 07:24.900
It's easy to cut the
veins in your body!

07:24.980 --> 07:26.600
You want me to do it?

07:27.450 --> 07:28.810
No, Brother!

07:28.880 --> 07:29.710
Don't!

07:30.080 --> 07:35.650
That's right. There's no way
you can do such a thing.

07:36.290 --> 07:38.980
The only one who could
do such a thing is me.

07:40.530 --> 07:41.580
Stop, please!

07:42.090 --> 07:44.360
We'll join you, so please stop!

07:44.500 --> 07:45.990
Don't do anything!

07:46.470 --> 07:47.520
Naoya...

07:47.870 --> 07:49.770
Is that so?

07:50.170 --> 07:54.940
If you did that from the beginning,
you wouldn't have had any problems.

08:14.760 --> 08:17.250
Sonezaki escaped...

08:20.830 --> 08:22.960
To think he escaped...

08:23.970 --> 08:25.960
You do not have to worry.

08:26.440 --> 08:27.530
But...

08:28.310 --> 08:31.440
...isn't it dangerous right
now to let Sonezaki out?

08:33.410 --> 08:36.610
When the time comes,
that man will end.

08:37.080 --> 08:39.110
It's not long now.

08:50.430 --> 08:51.620
Michio!

08:52.670 --> 08:53.930
Father...

08:54.900 --> 08:57.390
Michio, you were
causing mischief again.

08:57.500 --> 09:00.500
You are no good.
We can't do anything about you.

09:00.710 --> 09:04.870
I should have killed you before
you caused trouble to society.

09:05.280 --> 09:06.680
It's mother's fault.

09:06.750 --> 09:08.370
It's her fault!

09:08.480 --> 09:13.420
It's her fault that a
horrible guy like you was born!

09:14.950 --> 09:16.750
Shut up!

09:17.520 --> 09:18.850
You should just die!

09:18.920 --> 09:20.720
What! Try saying it one more time!

09:20.790 --> 09:22.760
Yeah, yeah, I'll say it
as many times as I need to!

09:22.830 --> 09:23.800
What!

09:32.140 --> 09:35.470
That's why I should have
killed you that time too.

09:38.540 --> 09:42.670
It's 'cause you were the slob!

09:42.820 --> 09:47.910
You didn't do anything on your own
and kept on blaming others!

09:49.090 --> 09:52.580
So all of that was genetically
transferred to you, huh?

10:24.060 --> 10:27.690
So Sonezaki, glad to see you again.

10:27.830 --> 10:29.590
K-Kamiya?

10:30.030 --> 10:34.400
Thank you for ending my life.

10:35.000 --> 10:39.300
You should hurry
over here too, Sonezaki.

10:44.640 --> 10:46.270
Thank you, Michio.

10:47.010 --> 10:50.680
Mother, I didn't do anything to you!

10:50.750 --> 10:52.440
What are you saying?

10:52.650 --> 10:58.610
It's because you controlled Father's
mind, so I was able to come over here.

11:07.630 --> 11:12.430
The last victim of your power is...

11:13.040 --> 11:14.530
...yourself...

11:41.700 --> 11:42.930
It's safe now.

11:43.470 --> 11:45.130
You weren't hurt, were you?

11:46.810 --> 11:48.000
Don't come near me, no!

11:48.070 --> 11:50.540
Please, please no more...

11:51.080 --> 11:52.540
Please leave!

11:52.610 --> 11:54.240
Y-You have it wrong!

11:54.310 --> 11:58.410
What's so fun about
picking on an old couple like us?

11:58.480 --> 12:00.210
Please forgive us!

12:02.150 --> 12:04.090
Mr. Kirihara, are you okay?

12:04.660 --> 12:07.720
We called the police.
They'll be coming soon.

12:08.830 --> 12:10.450
You have it wrong...

12:11.460 --> 12:12.660
Let's go, Naoya.

12:29.480 --> 12:33.210
Good-bye, Dad, Mom...

12:57.010 --> 12:57.770
Brother?

14:02.410 --> 14:04.430
People hate disputes...

14:04.510 --> 14:06.480
People prefer disputes...

14:07.080 --> 14:10.110
And if they do not
experience either of them...

14:10.180 --> 14:13.350
...they will not try to
conquer that sensation.

14:16.060 --> 14:19.580
That's what Shouko
whispered to me.

14:20.690 --> 14:23.060
Dispute, huh?

14:23.300 --> 14:25.990
Brother, they're coming closer...

14:26.530 --> 14:30.900
The people that feel that
our existence is in the way.

14:52.320 --> 14:54.660
Sonezaki is done.

14:55.190 --> 14:56.090
Yes.

14:57.760 --> 15:00.460
But he's in sheer bliss right now.

15:01.030 --> 15:03.930
He's taking a walk in nature.

15:10.540 --> 15:11.570
Sakaguchi.

15:11.880 --> 15:12.570
Yes.

15:13.250 --> 15:15.180
The time is coming closer.

15:16.620 --> 15:18.740
Something is going to
make a move tonight.

16:07.230 --> 16:09.220
<i>Naoto Kirihara, Psychokinesis
Naoya Kirihara, Reading
Neither have reached their full potential.</i>

16:09.300 --> 16:11.200
<i>Impossible to live a normal life.
Lived at Kyojiro Mikuriya's psychic
ability laboratory for 15 years.</i>

16:15.110 --> 16:19.010
<i>Shouko Okuhara foresaw the
Kirihara Brothers. The keyword was...</i>

16:20.680 --> 16:22.370
<i>Uncertain data</i>

16:22.880 --> 16:24.310
<i>Danger</i>

16:27.290 --> 16:31.550
<i>Absorption, otherwise elimination</i>

17:07.360 --> 17:09.050
<i>Unknown</i>

17:10.230 --> 17:11.390
Hello?

17:20.970 --> 17:22.130
Mr. Futami?

17:22.710 --> 17:23.770
Natsuko...

17:24.140 --> 17:25.070
...please forgive me.

17:25.610 --> 17:26.510
What?

18:00.750 --> 18:03.440
It's like it's taking
the place of telepathy.

18:03.980 --> 18:04.850
Huh?

18:05.120 --> 18:06.450
Cell phones.

18:06.850 --> 18:10.790
Nowadays, everything requires
a materialistic explanation.

18:11.090 --> 18:14.350
Without that, they will not
understand the phenomenon.

18:14.490 --> 18:16.890
That's how everyone's
consciousness is made now.

18:17.530 --> 18:21.860
A couple of years from now,
phones will become the size of beans.

18:22.130 --> 18:24.830
Or maybe from here on,
it will be normal for...

18:24.900 --> 18:29.500
...people to talk to each other
without having anything in their hands.

18:37.680 --> 18:39.710
Huh? My cell phone won't connect.

18:42.420 --> 18:43.910
Some kind of message...

18:44.460 --> 18:45.320
Naoya!

18:55.730 --> 19:01.430
About 10 minutes ago, the country's
TV, radio, cell phone, and internet...

19:01.640 --> 19:07.510
...networks were suspended for about
three seconds, causing mass confusion.

19:08.010 --> 19:10.480
The cause has not yet
been determined, but...

19:10.550 --> 19:13.950
...once we have more information,
we will report it immediately.

19:21.230 --> 19:22.280
It's here.

19:34.040 --> 19:39.980
He asked me to bring you guys here.

19:40.710 --> 19:42.540
Although he didn't use words...

20:03.240 --> 20:05.970
What was happening to him?

20:06.040 --> 20:08.130
Why a place like this...

20:26.730 --> 20:29.190
Yoshiki Futami, age 33.

20:29.290 --> 20:33.360
My birthday is June 30th, 1973.

20:33.430 --> 20:34.590
Futami...

20:35.270 --> 20:37.460
It's the same last name as Shouko.

20:37.700 --> 20:39.570
Is there some kind of connection?

20:39.810 --> 20:41.070
Shouko?

20:41.210 --> 20:42.330
I don't know her.

20:42.710 --> 20:45.840
The one that disconnected
the network was him!

20:46.080 --> 20:47.240
For what purpose?

20:47.450 --> 20:49.180
So he doesn't get tracked.

20:51.750 --> 20:55.380
Right now, I belong
to Ark Corporation.

20:55.590 --> 20:56.450
Ark...

20:56.520 --> 20:58.080
This is my employee ID.

20:58.160 --> 21:02.560
On the outside, we are a network
business company, but in reality, we're not.

21:02.730 --> 21:06.290
It's a mysterious company
doing a lot of things in the dark.

21:06.830 --> 21:09.100
The CEO's power is too strong.

21:09.470 --> 21:14.740
The movement of my mind and actions
are all managed by the CEO's power.

21:16.240 --> 21:20.140
But I devised a plan
to get away from that.

21:20.650 --> 21:24.100
And I was able to get
to this room secretly.

21:25.820 --> 21:28.410
This was possible
because I found a certain rule.

21:28.550 --> 21:32.720
The CEO's mind powers are
strong beyond measure, but...

21:32.790 --> 21:36.490
...there are moments that his
mind moves away from my actions.

21:38.930 --> 21:44.030
That's when the CEO's mind
focuses on two particular men.

21:44.670 --> 21:49.900
That's the only time I can
run from the mind surveillance.

21:50.640 --> 21:52.170
Those two are brothers.

21:55.610 --> 21:59.140
I'm guessing their
existence is that big.

21:59.750 --> 22:04.590
I weaved between the CEO's
mind and decided to record this.

22:04.860 --> 22:07.150
The abnormality that
has happened to me...

22:23.010 --> 22:25.770
No!

22:31.250 --> 22:34.510
<i>An exact answer is nowhere.</i>

22:34.590 --> 22:37.180
<i>Even if you corner it, it still runs.</i>

22:37.260 --> 22:41.850
<i>It's that kind of repeating all the time.</i>

22:41.930 --> 22:45.160
<i>We hurt each other
and rip each other apart.</i>

22:45.230 --> 22:47.860
<i>We're complaining once again.</i>

22:47.930 --> 22:53.270
<i>When tomorrow comes, just like a lie,
you wear a mask and live on.</i>

22:53.340 --> 22:58.640
<i>I was wishing upon
the night stars...</i>

22:58.710 --> 23:03.980
<i>...for our distance
to become shorter.</i>

23:04.050 --> 23:10.680
<i>But if I try to bluff,
then I'm going to regret it.</i>

23:10.760 --> 23:13.220
<i>Words and feelings are reverse.</i>

23:13.290 --> 23:18.850
<i>Feelings that were asleep,
heart that was asleep, lure it out!</i>

23:18.930 --> 23:24.200
<i>Glamour that was asleep, myself
that was asleep, with your power!</i>

23:24.270 --> 23:29.730
<i>Please look at me quietly with the soul
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:29.810 --> 23:34.610
<i>I want you to go wilder inside me.</i>

23:34.680 --> 23:40.140
<i>Eyes that were asleep, emotions
that were asleep, wake them up!</i>

23:40.220 --> 23:45.490
<i>Memories that were asleep, dreams
that were asleep, with your power!</i>

23:45.560 --> 23:51.020
<i>Please melt me with the vision of kindness
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:51.100 --> 23:58.200
<i>I want to stay asleep
longer buried inside you.</i>

24:00.770 --> 24:04.670
Behind the undesired struggle to the
death is the undesired conclusion.

24:05.680 --> 24:10.310
That is the cross you have to
carry for the rest of the way.

24:10.880 --> 24:14.080
The girl of guidance is
sent to another, higher level.

24:14.850 --> 24:17.010
The soul that struggles
and suffers wanders...

24:17.090 --> 24:19.220
...around the ominous electronic place...

24:19.290 --> 24:23.320
Eventually, screaming and
whispering all turn into silence.

24:24.300 --> 24:29.860
<i>Episode 18, "Ark"</i>

24:26.770 --> 24:29.860
Where are we headed?
